**Prefer `@ServiceConnection` for Neo4j.** It's the less verbose option, and Spring Boot has built-in support for `Neo4jContainer`. Use `@DynamicPropertySource` when you need more control. The docs call it "a slightly more verbose but also more flexible alternative" [S2].

## `@ServiceConnection`
You put the annotation on the container field. Spring Boot then defines a `Neo4jConnectionDetails` bean automatically. The Neo4j auto-configuration uses that bean, and it overrides any connection-related configuration properties [S12]. Connection details take precedence over properties in general [S12].

```java
@Testcontainers
@SpringBootTest
class MyIntegrationTests {

	@Container
	@ServiceConnection
	static Neo4jContainer neo4j = new Neo4jContainer("neo4j:5");
}
```

- You need `spring-boot-testcontainers` as a test dependency [S12].
- `ContainerConnectionDetailsFactory` classes, registered in `spring.factories`, process the annotation. They create the `ConnectionDetails` bean from the `Container` subclass or from the Docker image name [S12].
- The `Neo4jConnectionDetails` factory matches containers of type `Neo4jContainer` [S6].
- This also works on a `@Bean` method. Spring Boot uses the method's return type to pick the connection details, so a typed container like `Neo4jContainer` works [S13].

## `@DynamicPropertySource`
A static method adds property values to the Spring `Environment`, and you choose which properties to set [S2].

```java
@Container
static Neo4jContainer neo4j = new Neo4jContainer("neo4j:5");

@DynamicPropertySource
static void neo4jProperties(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
	registry.add("spring.neo4j.uri", neo4j::getBoltUrl);
}
```

The docs example only sets `spring.neo4j.uri` [S2]. I didn't find a passage showing how credentials are handled with this approach. If your container needs authentication, check that your test sets the `spring.neo4j.authentication.*` properties [S4].

## Summary

| | `@ServiceConnection` | `@DynamicPropertySource` |
|---|---|---|
| Mechanism | Creates a `Neo4jConnectionDetails` bean | Adds properties to the `Environment` |
| Precedence | Overrides connection properties | Sets properties like any other property source |
| Effort | Annotate the field | Write a method and map each property yourself |
| Flexibility | Limited to the supported connection details | You can set any property |

